          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: দেনা",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দেনা — denā — \"a debt (owed); what one owes\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দোকানদারের কাছে আমাদের কিছু দেনা আছে। dokāndārer kāchhe āmāder kichhu denā āchhe. We owe the shopkeeper some money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ধার is a loan; দেনা (denā) is what is still to be paid back."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দেনা (denā) is built on দে-, the stem of দেওয়া, to give, the Bengali verb that goes back to Sanskrit dadāti (Monier-Williams): what one has still to give."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
