            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেটানো — meṭāno — \"to settle (a bill); to make good\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "হোটেল ছাড়ার আগে আমরা বিল মেটালাম। hoṭel chhāṛār āge āmrā bil meṭālām. Before leaving the hotel we settled the bill."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he/she …): তিনি বিল মেটালেন, tini bil meṭālen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also of a quarrel or a need: ঝগড়া মেটানো (meṭāno), to settle a quarrel; খিদে মেটানো (meṭāno), to satisfy hunger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মেটানো (meṭāno) is the causing form of মেটা, which CDIAL lists as Bengali meṭā, \"to be wiped out\", under Sanskrit mṛṣṭá, \"rubbed, washed\" (CDIAL 10299): to settle a bill is to wipe it out."
            }
          ]
        },
